  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Biorefinery enzymes for renewable chemicals: from discovery to industrial applications</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Challenges Research Fund (GCRF) supports cutting-edge research to address challenges faced by developing countries. The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world. The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training award to upskill early career researchers from Thailand, Malaysia, Indonesia, Vietnam and the Philippines on the use of biorefinery enzymes in an industrial context. This will provide researchers with a multidisciplinary training that will enhance their careers, as well as improving academic-industry partnerships in these countries.</narrative>
  </description>
